\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP: Volatile Mkts, Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Raise Concern In HK \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kirsti Hastings \par \uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 1998\par 11:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The Hang Seng Index was rattled by the collapse of share prices worldwide, including a severe decline on Wall Street overnight, and news that Standard & Poor's had downgraded Hong Kong's sovereign rating. \par \par \uc2  But a wave of short-covering in the stock and stock futures market - some of it believed to have been generated by the government - kept the benchmark index from diving to new lows Tuesday and helped ease a fall in September Hang Seng Index futures. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Hang Seng Index fell only 212.57 points, or 2.9%, to close at 7062.47 in a volatile session. It moved between 6982.43 and 7306.40 points Tuesday. The September Hang Seng futures contract closed at 6810, down 190 points, narrowing its even steeper discount from just a few days ago. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Tuesday's market activity indicated the government seems to be winning its war against speculators, as open interest in the futures markets has been falling in the past few days. But many continue to criticize the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are no longer free. \par \par \uc2  Late Tuesday afternoon, money market dealers said the overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate fell sharply to 6% from 19% earlier in the day amid signs of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers said Hongkong & Shanghai Banking Corp. was pumping liquidity in the market on behalf of the government to drive rates lower and take pressure off the spot Hong Kong dollar and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg. \par \par \uc2  Neither the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  nor Hongkong Bank would comment on market activities. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 01-09-98 \par \par \uc2  0953GMT \par \par \uc2  1139 62560 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9107h10\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
