\par\par \b \uc2  Mkt Yawns/HK Downgrade -2: Govt Hits Back At Criticism \b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 1998\par 06:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  S&P joined the chorus of criticism leveled at the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  for using the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local stock and futures markets. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA in the stock market last week changes the mix of financial assets backing the Hong Kong dollar. By some estimates, the HKMA has already spent up to US$15 billion buying shares and futures as part of an increasingly complex, and risky, strategy to deter speculative pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," S&P said. \par \par \uc2  "As bearish sentiment against the Hong Kong dollar shows no signs of abating, further share purchases could follow. Once these \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  cease, however, HKMA's portfolio likely will suffer significant losses unless the downward trend in global equity prices is reversed," the ratings agency added. \par \par \uc2  The government, for its part, said in a statement that it "does not find S&P's decision to downgrade the credit ratings of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  justified." \par \par \uc2  "Government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the stocks and futures markets is to deter manipulation in these markets by speculators who are attacking the Hong Kong dollar at the same time," it added. \par \par \uc2  Debt market players say it's still a bad strategy. \par \par \uc2  "Now, everything the government is doing is wrong," said a Hong Kong-based trader who, like most of his colleagues, requested anonymity when commenting on the government's recent activity. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 01-09-98 \par \par \uc2  0412GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9107fbw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
