\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals withstand stronger dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 766 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 1998\par 11:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0925 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly steady as \par \par \uc2  the dollar remained capped below 142 yen after rising on news \par \par \uc2  that North Korea had fired a missile into the Sea of Japan. \par \par \uc2      The dollar rebounded sharply from a nine-month low of 1.73 \par \par \uc2  marks ahead of the Russian Duma's debate on the nomination of \par \par \uc2  Viktor Chernomyrdin as Prime Minister, due to begin at 1100 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2  President Boris Yeltsin's parliamentary envoy said Russia's \par \par \uc2  lower house of parliament was likely to reject Chernomyrdin's \par \par \uc2  confirmation vote. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had earlier come under heavy pressure against \par \par \uc2  the mark and Swiss franc as operators bailed out of long \par \par \uc2  positions amid signs Russia's leaders might be able to reach a \par \par \uc2  compromise, which would allow the government to deal with the \par \par \uc2  stricken economy. \par \par \uc2  *** But regional markets were more focused on a steep seven \par \par \uc2  percent drop in Hong Kong's blue chip Hang Seng Index and \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's planned measures to cope with its first recession in \par \par \uc2  13 years. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was well off its lows in thin offshore trade, \par \par \uc2  with Malaysian markets closed for the National Day holiday, and \par \par \uc2  overseas players speculating on the possible imposition of some \par \par \uc2  form of capital controls. \par \par \uc2  The Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange called a news conference \par \par \uc2  for 0900 GMT and government officials said a special cabinet \par \par \uc2  meeting would be held on Tuesday morning to discuss economic \par \par \uc2  measures. \par \par \uc2  Rumours swirling through \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets ranged from \par \par \uc2  speculation Malaysia might impose a two-tier \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  system to renewed talk Finance Minister Anwar Ibrahim planned \par \par \uc2  to resign. \par \par \uc2  The official Bernama news agency quoted Anwar as denying \par \par \uc2  that he was tendering his resignation or that he would resign \par \par \uc2  on Friday. \par \par \uc2  *** Hong Kong's stock market ended sharply lower as the \par \par \uc2  government retreated somewhat from its recent aggressive \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar firmed in both spot and forward \par \par \uc2  markets as the overnight interbank rate jumped on a sharp \par \par \uc2  increase in demand for short-term funds after the Hong Kong \par \par \uc2  Futures Exchange said it would levy a margin surcharge. \par \par \uc2  On Saturday, the HKFE imposed a 150 percent margin \par \par \uc2  surcharge on large Hang Seng futures positions above 10,000 \par \par \uc2  contracts. \par \par \uc2  *** In Thailand, the baht was off its lows, with traders \par \par \uc2  brushing off news that the country's trade surplus narrowed to \par \par \uc2  $928 million in June from $949 million in May, and compared \par \par \uc2  with a $920 million deficit in June last year. \par \par \uc2      Imports were down a massive 35.9 percent year-on-year, \par \par \uc2  while exports dipped some three percent. \par \par \uc2      The current account surplus narrowed to a preliminary $853 \par \par \uc2  million in June from $1.01 billion in May and a $870 million \par \par \uc2  deficit last June. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won weakened on heavy corporate dollar \par \par \uc2  demand ahead of import settlements early next month, with \par \par \uc2  dealers shrugging off the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement that it \par \par \uc2  would cut the rediscount rate by 200 basis points to three \par \par \uc2  percent in a bid to boost the economy. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the impact of the North Korean missile news \par \par \uc2  was limited, as were growing expectations that an international \par \par \uc2  auction for ailing Kia Motors and sister firm Asia Motors would \par \par \uc2  be cancelled after bidders demanded better terms on the firms' \par \par \uc2  mountains of debt. \par \par \uc2  *** The Singapore dollar briefly fell to the wrong side of \par \par \uc2  1.78 to the U.S. dollar following a local newspaper report \par \par \uc2  quoting eight private-sector forecasters saying it could drop \par \par \uc2  as low as 1.85 by year-end. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Sing dollar was likely to remain under \par \par \uc2  pressure from a perception that Singapore authorities might be \par \par \uc2  willing to tolerate further weakness in the domestic dollar and \par \par \uc2  fears oil-rich Brunei, which pegs its dollar to the Sing, might \par \par \uc2  be facing financial difficulty. \par \par \uc2       Change on the day MON 31 0928GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest.....Prev Close...Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit....4.19.........4.23.........0.95% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah.....10725.00.....10750.00.....0.23% \par \par \uc2   Baht.......41.78........41.90........0.29% \par \par \uc2   Peso.......43.90........43.91........0.02% \par \par \uc2   Sing Dlr...1.78.........1.78.........0.03% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan Dlr.34.84........34.83.......-0.04% \par \par \uc2   Korean Won.1348.00......1332.00.....-1.19% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest.....July '97