\par\par \b \uc2  Taiwan says won't tap reserves to shore up stocks. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lawrence Chung \par \uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 1998\par 13:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TAIPEI, Aug 31 (Reuters) - Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday again ruled out using \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to shore up the stock market, saying the island's mountainous reserves could be mobilised only to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It's unlikely we would use our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to hold the stock market despite its recent declines," bank vice governor Hsu Yi-hsiung said after the financial markets closed. \par \par \uc2  Hsu spoke in response to unconfirmed media reports that funds linked to U.S. financer George Soros had turned to Taiwan after being rebuffed in Hong Kong, where the government has supported the stock market with a huge buying campaign. \par \par \uc2  Hsu said Taiwan's financial system differed from that of Hong Kong and that the island's reserves would be used only in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stockpile, ranking among the world's 10 largest, stood at US$83.607 at the end of July. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong is thought to have used one-seventh of its US$90 billion-plus hoard of reserves and land funds in a blistering and uncharacteristic defence of its stock market. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong financial officials said the defence aimed to thwart speculative international funds from manipulating the stock market to undermine the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  State \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect Taiwan's stock market is an open secret, and Hsu declined to specify how this is done. \par \par \uc2  Brokers say Taipei typically deploys major funds under its control, including pension and labour insurance funds, to buy stocks in the face of what its officials deem unwarranted selling. \par \par \uc2  The most conspicuous recent example came in early 1996 when intimidating war games and missile tests mounted by Taiwan's arch rival, communist China, sent Taiwan investors fleeing the stock market and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the safety of U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rolled out Taiwan's reserves to defend the Taiwan dollar, but the finance ministry and other organs set up separate emergency funds that were deployed to keep a floor under the sagging stock market. \par \par \uc2  Since Asia's financial crisis erupted in mid-1997, Taiwan's index has fallen some 27 percent and state-linked buying became active in the past week as it has tumbled to 22-month lows. \par \par \uc2  Shock over Hong Kong's seven percent tumble on Monday sent Taiwan's index for a 2.76 percent slide to 6,550.11, its lowest close since October 1996. \par \par \uc2  Hsu said it was relatively unlikely for international speculators to attack Taiwan given its stronger economic fundamentals and floating exchange rate. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  director Chou Ah-ting said on Monday he was confident international speculators would find little quarter to attack Taiwan's markets. \par \par \uc2  "Don't be scared by Soros. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not fear him," Chou said. \par \par \uc2  Chou said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  checks found no obvious presence of funds controlled by Soros or other funds in Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - despite rumours to this effect. \par \par \uc2  In any case, they were unwelcome in Taiwan, he said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stringently monitor the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market so that such speculators will find no quarter to operate here," Chou said. ((Taipei newsroom, +886 2 2508-0815 fax +886 2 2508-0204, taipei.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8v01vbu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
