\par\par \b \uc2  HK Late Hibor Higher On Tight Liquidity, Weakness In HK$ \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 1998\par 09:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates rose late Friday, as pressure on the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued and liquidity in local money markets dried up. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate was quoted at 20.0% late Friday, up from 18.0% late in the previous session. The three-month rate was 16.0%, up from 14.0% late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market was strapped for cash and the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't injected any liquidity. \par \par \uc2  In addition, with the Hong Kong dollar nearing the key level of HK$7.75 to the U.S. dollar, traders said the government probably is willing to let interest rates stay high to help support the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the past, the HKMA has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it approached the HK$7.75 level. \par \par \uc2  Around 0746 GMT (3:45 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7499 per U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7460 recorded late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Forward premiums also rose late Friday, indicating speculative pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is increasing. Late Friday, the one-year premium was quoted at 7700 points, up from 6200 points early in the session and much higher than 5700 late in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  Due to Hong Kong's modified \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, weakness in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  leads automatically to higher interest rates. However, the HKMA has also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and adjust interest rates. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 28-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0755GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8s07bfb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
