\par\par \b \uc2  HK  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  not a factor in credit review - S&P. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christopher Kaufman \par \uc2 449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 13:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Aug 27 (Reuters) - Rating agency Standard and Poor's Corp said on Thursday \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the equity cash and futures markets was not having a significant impact on its review of the territory's credit rating. \par \par \uc2  S&P Managing Director for Hong Kong Paul Coughlin said depressed conditions in the Asian region and their effect on the Hong Kong economy through its U.S. dollar-linked exchange rate were more likely to lead to a downgrade than the actions of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA). \par \par \uc2  "If the conditions in the region persist, you would expect the disinflation to be transmitted through the peg into the Hong Kong economy," Coughlin said in an interview aired on Reuters Television on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "What the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is doing now doesn't affect that one way or another," he said. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the equity cash and futures markets on August 14 in an effort to force speculators to abandon short stock positions. \par \par \uc2  Its action has drawn heavy criticism from market participants who fear the new \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance has scared away genuine investment in the battered markets of Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  S&P's Coughlin said the agency was more concerned with the big picture than daily market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I don't think we necessarily get overly focused or overly sort of fixated on a single tactic," he said. \par \par \uc2  Disinflation, a slowing down of the rate at which prices increase, has been evident in Hong Kong, where consumer prices are rising at the slowest rate in 12 years. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Hong Kong asset prices are crumbling, with both property and share prices off about 50 percent from 1997 peaks. \par \par \uc2  And Coughlin warned that as disinflation moved more deeply through the economy affecting nominal wages, then "the capacity (of people) to repay loans to the banks themselves could be more significantly impacted," causing greater stress in the financial sector, he said. \par \par \uc2  Coughlin said the Hong Kong dollar's linked exchange rate with the U.S. dollar could be the key conduit of disinflation. \par \par \uc2  As pressures on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mount, interest rates automatically rise through the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, dampening economic growth and keeping price increases at bay. \par \par \uc2  He said S&P is examining "to what extent the peg and its effect are fundamentally undermining the considerable strengths of Hong Kong's corporate and banking sectors." \par \par \uc2  S&P put Hong Kong on CreditWatch with negative implications on June 22. \par \par \uc2  - Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6935; Fax (852) 2845-0636 \par \par \uc2  - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8r01og8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
