\par\par \b \uc2  HK Midday Hibor Higher As Liquidity Crunch Continues \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 05:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates are higher midday Thursday as tight liquidity forces up short-term lending rates \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 15.0%, up from 9.875% late Wednesday, and from 14.5% early in the session. \par \par \uc2  The three-month rate is 13.0%, up from 12.375% late Wednesday, and from 12.75% early Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a local bank said there's no sign of any let-up in the liquidity crunch, which is believed to be the government's latest tactic against speculators targeting the Hong Kong dollar by shorting the Hang Seng Index. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock market in a bid to squeeze out speculators in recent weeks. The HKMA, the territory's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on market activities. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they suspect the government is deliberately keeping liquidity tight before releasing cash through selected banks to lend to borrowers with genuine commercial need for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They said Russian turmoil is finally filtering through to affect sentiment in the money market. If the Russian ruble's woes hit emerging markets' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Hong Kong dollar, will probably come under renewed pressure, pushing up interest rates. \par \par \uc2  In the futures market, the September three-month Hibor contract is quoted at 87.75 for an underlying money market yield of 12.25%. Only 200 lots have been traded. \par \par \uc2  At 0300 GMT (11:00 p.m. EDT Wednesday), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7490 per U.S. dollar, weaker than HK$7.7461 recorded late Wednesday and HK$7.7487 to the U.S. dollar early in the current session. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 27-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0336GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8r07c78\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
