\par\par \b \uc2  US Economist Krugman Defends HK Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 : Report \b0\par\par\uc2 191 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 02:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--U.S. economist Paul Krugman defended the Hong Kong government's recent meddling in the stock and stock futures markets, despite wide criticism that the moves violate Hong Kong's reputation as a free market economy, according to an interview published in Thursday's South China Morning Post. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock and stock futures markets for nearly two weeks as part of an effort to thwart speculative attacks on the markets and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Krugman told the Post that if international hedge funds have been deliberately manipulating \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial markets, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was justifiable. \par \par \uc2  "It looks to me as if this stock market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the only instrument available," Krugman said, according to the English-language daily. \par \par \uc2  The stock market's benchmark Hang Seng Index has gained 18% since the government first stepped into the market. The moves have sent investors who shorted the markets scurrying, traders say. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 27-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0037GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8r07bms\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
