\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Steady Late As HK Battles For Econ Stability \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 11:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar late Thursday was nearly flat from Wednesday's level after rising steadily off a weak opening. \par \par \uc2  "It's been steadily bought all day," said a trader at a British bank. Much of the buying was by investors hoping to take advantage of high Hong Kong interest rates and by speculators covering short positions, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0820 GMT (4:20 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7460 against the U.S. dollar, marginally stronger than the HK$7.7461 quoted late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar has traded in a range of HK$7.7450 and HK$7.7494 so far Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 18.00%, up sharply from 9.875% late Wednesday. The three-month rate is 14.00%, up from 12.375% Wednesday. For more Hibor news, please refer to Telerate page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  Market players were focusing on two things, traders said: the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local stock market and the Russian ruble. \par \par \uc2  The Russian government on Wednesday stopped supporting the ruble and many investors fear a ruble free fall will send other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbling, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In addition, many investors are nervous about how high the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  can drive the Hang Seng Index Friday. The HKMA has been buying shares in both the cash and futures markets for a week to drive up prices and squeeze out speculators who had shorted the Hong Kong dollar and shares. The August futures contract expires Friday, and the higher the HKMA drives it, the more pain it can inflict. \par \par \uc2  "The next couple of days will be critical for the whole world," said one trader, as Russia and Hong Kong battle for economic stability. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 27-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0938GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8r079yz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
