\par\par \b \uc2  Economists/HK$ Peg -2: Speculators Spot A Paradox \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 11:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  But the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly bought the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , blue-chip stocks and stock futures over the past few weeks to lift local markets. While the government says the action is aimed at driving out speculators who had taken short positions, critics say it shows it isn't willing to let the economy bear the pain of rising rates and falling asset prices. \par \par \uc2  They also argue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is delaying economic adjustment necessary to restore \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's competitiveness and pull the domestic economy out of its first recession in 13 years, and will eventually lead the government to abandon the peg because of the heavy price of defending it. \par \par \uc2  "You can maintain a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board if you let it function," Wood said. "The only way...to hold it in place, is if the government is to give a consistently strong message it is willing to bear the pain. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactics we're seeing are the opposite of that." \par \par \uc2  Indeed, critics say Hong Kong's credibility as a free and open financial center is fading fast as the government's foray into markets and efforts to justify the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue, economists say. \par \par \uc2  In an opinion piece earlier this week, HKMA Chief Executive Joseph Yam Chi-kwong sought to counter mounting criticism of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , urging the G-7 economies to join in or end up picking up the bill for bailing out weak emerging market economies. \par \par \uc2  But most economists doubt the government's effort will drive off speculators permanently. \par \par \uc2  "I think that the idea that you can scare off speculators is a false one," BZW Asia economist Kate O'Donohugh says. "They've spotted a trend, a paradox, in what's happening and they're trying to exploit that. You can't get rid of speculators until you get rid of that paradox." \par \par \uc2  The strident voices against the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are saying the government is leading \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  down a ruinous path. August's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock, stock futures and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets follows the its attempt to stabilize the property market in June by suspending its land sales program for the rest of the fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 27-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0937GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8r079yl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
