\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals weaker as yen sags. \b0\par\par\uc2 817 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 04:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0100 GMT - The Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were easier in \par \par \uc2  morning trading as dollar/yen got back to the 144.50 level. \par \par \uc2      The absence of many fresh factors has seen the regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  again start to move in lock-step with the yen's \par \par \uc2  moves. \par \par \uc2      Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue to hold back dollar/yen but \par \par \uc2  some analysts are saying that the authorities are more \par \par \uc2  interested in the level of the Nikkei than the level of \par \par \uc2  dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  A further fall in the Nikkei would further pressure ailing \par \par \uc2  banks and some analysts believe it will be a fall in the Nikkei \par \par \uc2  that will be more instrumental in prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather \par \par \uc2  than a fall in the yen. \par \par \uc2      *** The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was under pressure with the \par \par \uc2  overnight rate jumping to 20 percent from 10 percent yesterday. \par \par \uc2      The was a subsequent kick-up in the forwards with \par \par \uc2  six-months at 2,750/2,950. Spot Hong Kong was at 7.7430/40. \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah was a little easier in line with the general \par \par \uc2  trend but it is still on track for 10,000 as aid dollars flow \par \par \uc2  into the country. \par \par \uc2      The IMF approved a $1 billion loan payment to Indonesia \par \par \uc2  under its global rescue package, rewarding Jakarta for tough \par \par \uc2  reforms to rein in its worst economic crisis. \par \par \uc2      The Washington-based lending agency assembled a $41 billion \par \par \uc2  bailout for Jakarta in 1997 but after economic conditions \par \par \uc2  deteriorated in May the IMF and other donors agreed in July to \par \par \uc2  increase the amount of lending by $6 billion. \par \par \uc2  *** The ringgit was also easier in line with the general \par \par \uc2  trend it also reacted badly to an unexpectedly sharp fall in \par \par \uc2  profit at Malaysia's biggest bank. \par \par \uc2  Malayan Banking or Maybank reported net profit for its \par \par \uc2  financial year to June had plunged to 129.61 million ringgit \par \par \uc2  from 1.322 billion ringgit in the previous financial year. \par \par \uc2      Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast 1997/98 net profit \par \par \uc2  of 577 million ringgit. \par \par \uc2      *** The Thai baht was easier but offshore demand to settle \par \par \uc2  forward contracts should help underpin it in the days to come, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Thailand has said it will close off its \par \par \uc2  remaining forward/dollar swaps in September and counterparty \par \par \uc2  banks will need baht to settle. \par \par \uc2      The forwards were taken out when the BOT was trying to \par \par \uc2  defend the baht last year. \par \par \uc2      Thailand has said its worst recession in half a century \par \par \uc2  could be over within a year barring further shocks from the \par \par \uc2  rest of Asia. \par \par \uc2      Its fifth letter of intent to the IMF, approved by the \par \par \uc2  cabinet on Tuesday, said the nation's economy would post modest \par \par \uc2  growth in 1999 after contracting about seven percent in 1998. \par \par \uc2      An additional contigency budget amounting to 0.5 percent of \par \par \uc2  GDP would be set aside in 1998/1999 to help the government \par \par \uc2  finance the cost of banking sector reforms. \par \par \uc2     Analysts said the revised government forecasts were largely \par \par \uc2  in line with expectations but expressed some disappointment \par \par \uc2  that the government did not plan to widen further the budget \par \par \uc2  deficit. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won eased marginally on thin volume as \par \par \uc2  traders remained cautious over Russia. \par \par \uc2      But dealers said the won should be well supported as they \par \par \uc2  expected month-end dollar sales by exporters to kick in. \par \par \uc2      South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said earlier the \par \par \uc2  country's GDP was estimated to have contracted by around five \par \par \uc2  percent during the first half of 1998 from a year ago. \par \par \uc2      *** In the Philippines, the peso succumbed to month-end \par \par \uc2  demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2      Traders said renewed weakness in the yen and concerns about \par \par \uc2  the Russian rouble were pressuring the market. \par \par \uc2      The peso also slipped on market perception that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might not be able to prop it up. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said Bangko Sentral had been selling dollars in \par \par \uc2  recent sessions to help the peso. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has denied \par \par \uc2  such talk. \par \par \uc2      But with a lack of dollar supply in the market and the yen \par \par \uc2  back at 144, they said it was unlikely the peso would get much \par \par \uc2  support from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Change on the day WED 26 0236GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest.....Prev Close...Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit....4.21.........4.21..........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah.....11200.00.....10700.00.....-4.46% \par \par \uc2   Baht.......41.67........41.52........-0.36% \par \par \uc2   Peso.......43.67........43.25........-0.96% \par \par \uc2   Sing Dlr...1.78.........1.77.........-0.34% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan Dlr.34.82........34.81........-0.01% \par \par \uc2   Korean Won.1307.50......1306.00......-0.11% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest.....July '97.....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit....4.21.........2.52.......-40.14% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah.....11200.00.....2432.00....-78.29% \par \par \uc2   Baht.......41.67........25.90......-37.84% \par \par \uc2   Peso.......43.67........26.50......-39.32% \par \par \uc2   Sing Dlr...1.78.........1.43.......-19.48% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan Dlr.34.82........27.75......-20.29% \par \par \uc2   Korean Won.1307.50......842.00.....-35.60% \par \par \uc2   - Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840 \par \par \uc2   - Email: asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8q01jjq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
