\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong \highlight\uc2  Officials Explain Market  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Fund Managers \b0\par\par\uc2  By Erik Guyot, Staff Reporter \par \uc2 219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 07:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones Online News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- Senior government officials held a private meeting Tuesday with fund managers to explain the government's new policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock market to drive out \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators, according to Stephen Ho, a fund manager at AIG Investment Corp. (Asia) Ltd. who was present at the meeting. \par \par \uc2  Ho told Dow Jones Newswires the fund managers were briefed by Raphael Hui, Secretary for Financial Services, and Albert Lam, an official from the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  or HKMA. \par \par \uc2  Since Aug. 14, the HKMA has been buying Hong Kong shares to thwart \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators from simultaneously selling short stocks and attacking the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been criticized by some international investors. \par \par \uc2  "Some of the fund managers felt we should hear it from the horse's mouth," said Ho. The fund manager said the government officials reiterated their public statements that they would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when they see speculators attacking both \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stock market and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Ho said government officials wouldn't go into the details of their \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  or how much money they have spent. Ho also said he was generally supportive of the government's policy. \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1998 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020329du8q016rj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
