\par\par \b \uc2  HK Hibor Down Late After Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 10:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank rates were down late Wednesday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after an early morning spike in the overnight rate. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 9.875%, down from 12.00% late Tuesday, but well off its level of 20.00% early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark three-month rate is 12.375%, down from 13.00 late Tuesday, but unchanged from early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they suspect the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  lent some money at 18.00% to 19.00% early Wednesday after the sudden rate spike, helping bring rates down. An HKMA spokesman said the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on market activities. \par \par \uc2  However, some traders said the government could be becoming more active in the money market as part of its strategy against speculators of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Others disagree. Howard Gorges, a director at South China Securities Ltd. said he suspects the government deliberately let the overnight rate hit 20% to keep the heat on speculators by keeping their cost of funds high. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a European bank said he doesn't expect interbank rates to ease significantly further ahead of the expiry of the September Hang Seng Index futures contract. \par \par \uc2  The government is believed to be tussling with speculators in both the futures and the cash index ahead of the expiry Friday of the August contract. \par \par \uc2  Late Wednesday, the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7460 per U.S. dollar, barely changed from the HK$7.7457 recorded late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 26-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0858GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8q079oc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
