\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS - Govt action in Asia markets rings alarms. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Valerie Lee \par \uc2 827 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 1998\par 08:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 23 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by some \par \par \uc2  Asian governments to support their stock markets and fend off \par \par \uc2  speculators has received the thumbs-down from most analysts, \par \par \uc2  who say governments should keep clear of markets or risk \par \par \uc2  getting their fingers burned. \par \par \uc2  Investors gave a clear signal late last week, taking profit \par \par \uc2  after sharp rallies in markets in Kuala Lumpur, Hong Kong and \par \par \uc2  Taiwan earlier in the week on talk of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At the close of trade on Friday, several Asian markets had \par \par \uc2  surrendered the week's gains with Malaysia's key Composite \par \par \uc2  Index tumbling 7.69 percent as investors cashed out. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously, investors will be disappointed because they \par \par \uc2  hate surprise elements and if the governments try to manage the \par \par \uc2  market it is not taken very positively," said Nilesh Jasani, a \par \par \uc2  regional strategist with SG Securities in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "The alarm bells always go off a bit when you hear about \par \par \uc2  governments propping up the markets because you are never quite \par \par \uc2  sure where the real floor is," said Peter Douglas, Director of \par \par \uc2  Aberdeen Asset Management in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said government-backed buying of shares would \par \par \uc2  bring out sellers eager to liquidate their holdings at the \par \par \uc2  expense of the regional authorities. It could also hurt the \par \par \uc2  long-term investor outlook for the markets involved, as risk \par \par \uc2  premiums for these markets would rise, they added. \par \par \uc2  "What is more, you are not addressing the real issues, you \par \par \uc2  are just swirling money around in the economy," said Kevin Gin, \par \par \uc2  a director with Kleinwort Benson Securities. "It's taking money \par \par \uc2  from out of one pocket and putting it into another," he said. \par \par \uc2  In recent weeks, several Asian governments either stepped \par \par \uc2  into their battered share markets as buyers or announced their \par \par \uc2  intention to use public funds to stimulate markets that are \par \par \uc2  drastically weaker than they were before the Asian financial \par \par \uc2  crisis flared up a year ago. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  started things, repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in stocks \par \par \uc2  and future markets after leader Tung Chee-hwa said the \par \par \uc2  government would step in if speculators attacked the Hong Kong \par \par \uc2  dollar and pushed interest rates higher while holding short \par \par \uc2  stock positions. In Malaysia, Prime Minister Mahathir \par \par \uc2  Mohamad said last week that a fund that subsidises the annual \par \par \uc2  pilgrimages of Malaysian Muslims to Saudi Arabia might \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy shares on behalf of the government. \par \par \uc2  Malaysian Deputy Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim said the huge \par \par \uc2  Employees' Pension Fund (EPF), could also step in. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan also said its securities watchdog, the Securities \par \par \uc2  and Futures Commission, was drafting various proposals to \par \par \uc2  stabilise the stock market. \par \par \uc2  Investors said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might succeed as \par \par \uc2  the government was not committed to defending a specific level \par \par \uc2  on the key Hang Seng share index. But the win would not come \par \par \uc2  without a price. \par \par \uc2  "It is not coming cheap. What it means is that the \par \par \uc2  government is not going through the mechanism of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  board," said a European investment house strategist, who \par \par \uc2  declined to be named. \par \par \uc2  "It is going outside it, which means that risk premiums on \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong in future will go up," he said, adding that the \par \par \uc2  country's reputation as perhaps the freest financial market in \par \par \uc2  Asia had been compromised. \par \par \uc2  Another issue was also whether or not the regional \par \par \uc2  authorities had deep enough pockets to sustain their support of \par \par \uc2  the markets as sellers continue to emerge, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "...the market will cap any artificially generated boost to \par \par \uc2  the asset markets," London-based research house I.D.E.A. said \par \par \uc2  in its regional markets focus on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "In the near-term, some caution may be evident in shorting \par \par \uc2  the indices and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but over a longer time frame \par \par \uc2  (bearish) fundamentals are seen winning through," it said. \par \par \uc2  But at least one investor said regional authorities were \par \par \uc2  entitled to take protective measures. \par \par \uc2  "A government has a social objective at the end of the day. \par \par \uc2  If you are a government, you have been elected, you have a \par \par \uc2  social objective and if investors are getting unreasonable you \par \par \uc2  have to act," said Jean Paolo Guarnieri, a director with \par \par \uc2  Salomon Borthers Asset Management in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "All this excitement from investors against the government \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a little bit naive. When you deal in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets around the world, for example, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always there....the  objective of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \par \par \uc2  not always mercantile," he said. \par \par \uc2  Percentage change in index levels since start of Asia \par \par \uc2  crisis: \par \par \uc2  Market............Current.........July 1997.........Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia\tab    388.35\tab     731.00 -46.9 pct\par Malaysia\tab     324.06\tab     1230.00 -73.7 pct\par Philippines\tab 1372.60\tab     2815.00 -51.2 pct\par Singapore\tab    933.16\tab     1981.00 -52.9 pct\par Thailand\tab     238.92\tab      569.00 -58.0 pct\par Hong Kong\tab   7527.61\tab    15055.00 -50.0 pct\par Japan\tab      15298.20\tab    20000.00 -23.5 pct\par Taiwan\tab      7213.37\tab     9000.00 -19.9 pct\par Korea\tab \tab  316.62\tab      770.00 -58.9 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (US$1.00=Malaysia $4.20).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8n01clz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
