\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - HK Newspaper Headlines - Aug 21. \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1998\par 03:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Aug 21 (Reuters) - These are some of the leading stories in Hong Kong newspapers on Friday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  SOUTH CHINA MORNING POST - Another brash government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the index futures market on Thursday failed to shake out many short positions, suggesting hedge funds are prepared for a long, tough battle, according to brokers. \par \par \uc2  - The Hong Kong Futures Exchange is considering demanding all margin payments be settled in Hong Kong dollars - a move interpreted by the market as a way of forcing international speculators to buy the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  even though they are shorting it. \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG STANDARD - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators on Thursday began unwinding some of their positions, suggesting that the government's strategy of preventing attacks on the Hong Kong dollar might be paying off. \par \par \uc2  - Final approval of a scheme allowing foreign banks in Shenzhen to engage in yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to be given by the State Council in the fourth quarter of this year, according to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official. \par \par \uc2  - HSBC Holdings Plc's  Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corp Ltd said it was well prepared to operate yuan business in Shenzhen. \par \par \uc2  MING PAO DAILY NEWS - Sincere Co Ltd  will lay off 70 employees, about 10 percent of the workforce, from September 1, and senior executives will have a salary cut of 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  - An explosion in a restaurant in northern China's Dalian port city killed two people. \par \par \uc2  APPLE DAILY - Dah Sing Financial Holdings Ltd  is studying the feasibility of merging with two other banks, according to a report by Jardine Fleming Securities. \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG ECONOMIC JOURNAL - Fund managers said government had asked them not to lend stocks to speculators for short selling. \par \par \uc2  - Hong Kong government intends to issue more fixed network telephone licences. \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG ECONOMIC TIMES - The Shenzhen branch of the People's Bank of China is studying a plan to extend loans to Hong Kong's small to medium enterprises in Shenzhen without requiring collateral or a guarantor. \par \par \uc2  WEN WEI PO - People's Bank of China deputy governor Liu Mingkan said the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not oppose the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock and futures market. \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Newsroom (852) 2843 6441; Fax (852) 2845 0636 \par \par \uc2  - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8l019cy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
