\par\par \b \uc2  HK 3-Month Hibor -3: Venezuela Devaluation Rumors \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1998\par 04:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Also hurting sentiment is a report of a default this week by a Russian borrower. The report quoted bankers as saying that a total of 13 syndicated loans to Russian borrowers will mature during a 90-day debt moratorium imposed by the Russian government earlier this week, and the first borrower went into default this week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums are up early Friday, partly in an attempt to push up interbank rates. "I wouldn't call it pure hedging. There's a speculative element," a local dealer said. \par \par \uc2  A local bank treasurer said the market is also roiled by rumors of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation in a Latin American economy. The Venezuelan government overnight denied any plans to devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bolivar. \par \par \uc2  The treasurer said a devaluation would put more pressure on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Hong Kong dollar, which could again test HK$7.75, seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Early Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is quoted at HK$7.7495 per U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7483 recorded late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org; \par \par \uc2  and Kate Pound Dawson \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0202GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8l0749g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\p