\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Opens -3: Buyers Pushing Up Interbank Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1998\par 03:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a European bank said he suspects the buying in the forward market originates with the same players who took big positions in earlier rates. He said he believes the buyers are trying to push up Hong Kong rates through the forwards. \par \par \uc2  The local bank treasurer said the rumor of a possible bolivar devaluation would put more pressure on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Hong Kong dollar which could again test HK$7.75, seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Interbank Offered Rates is quoted at 9.50%, compared with 8.875% late Thursday. The three-month rate is 11.25% from 10.125%. For more Hibor news, please refer to Telerate page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the six-month premium is quoted at 2,400 points, up from 2,200 previously. The one-year premium is quoted at 4,800 points, up from 4,600 previously. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org and Kate Pound Dawson \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0155GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8l07497\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
