\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA's Yam defends share market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 08:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Aug 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) chief Joseph Yam on Thursday defended the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock market and called on the world's financial leaders to consider that markets could be wrong. \par \par \uc2  Last Friday, Financial Secretary Donald Tsang said the government had asked the HKMA to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock and futures markets to deter \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation by speculators that had built up short positions in Hang Seng Index futures. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to have continued each trading day since Friday and has helped to drive up the stock market by more than 14 percent since last Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  In a lengthy letter to the Asian Wall Street Journal, Yam said there had been "quiet support" for Tsang's decision as well as "vehement criticism" on grounds the action violated Hong Kong's free market philosophy and demonstrated the government's unwillingness to suffer the pain of economic adjustment under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system. \par \par \uc2  Yam said the criticism was misplaced. \par \par \uc2  He reiterated that the government had no objection to anyone, including hedge funds, taking short positions in stock index futures and reaping the benefits of Hong Kong's asset price adjustment. \par \par \uc2  But he said it was clear that speculators were engaged in a "double play" of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation with the specific aim of pushing stock prices lower, with no regard to the asset adjustments that had already taken place. \par \par \uc2  "This presents serious risks of markets overshooting, with asset markets ratcheting down on every occasion the manipulators engage in this activity," said Yam. \par \par \uc2  Yam said the rising Hong Kong dollar interest rate risk premium had been unfairly attributed to fears the government would discard the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, when in fact a large portion of the premium was caused by the manipulators' actions. \par \par \uc2  "I do not know how many times we expressed the view that we have to stick it out and bear the inevitable pain, and that a fixed exchange rate under our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system is the best option for Hong Kong," Yam said. \par \par \uc2  "But it is unfair to ask the community to put up with excessive pain inflicted on it by those engaged in this double play of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock futures markets," he said. \par \par \uc2  Yam said the government had agonized over the decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "We were acutely aware of the possibility of our action being misunderstood," he said. \par \par \uc2  Yam said the government's resolve in adhering to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system had "never been stronger," saying there was no other alternative for Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  "Financial liberalisation and the globalisation of financial markets has left little scope for a small open economy to pursue flexible exchange rates," he said, adding that allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to float was not even a viable long-term alternative. \par \par \uc2  Yam said the government had not departed from strict observance of the monetary rule of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board despite the HKMA's recent buying of Hong Kong dollars for the treasury. \par \par \uc2  "Adherence to monetary rule does not preclude the government funding a budget deficit by drawing down its fiscal reserves that are held in foreign assets in the Exchange Fund," he said. \par \par \uc2  It also did not "preclude a portfolio shift outside the balance sheet of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board from other assets into Hong Kong stocks for whatever purposes considered to be in the best interests of Hong Kong," Yam said. \par \par \uc2  Yam also called into question the accepted wisdom that markets cannot be wrong and that governments generally are wrong. If this were always the case, he said, "why are we witnessing the emerging markets shaking themselves to bits?" \par \par \uc2  "If emerging markets continue to devalue their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which some commentators still suggest is inevitable, the costs will be borne either through massive deflation in the developing world or bubbles in the developed markets, or both," he said. \par \par \uc2  Yam said there was a need to get a message to industrialised nations that abstaining from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain global financial market stability, especially \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability, may no longer be a viable option. \par \par \uc2  Yam's comments appeared on the paper's editorial page. \par \par \uc2  - Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371; Fax (852) 2845-0636 - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8k017he\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
