\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA Says Fight Against Speculators To Drag On - Report \b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 03:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The territory's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects to maintain its pressure on speculators for a long time, a local newspaper reported Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "We will continue these actions until the speculators have completely left the Hong Kong market," the South China Morning Post quoted Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief executive Joseph Yam as saying. \par \par \uc2  "We (the HKMA) have to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock and futures markets until the speculators have wound up their short positions," Yam was quoted as saying. \par \par \uc2  Since last week, the government has been buying blue-chip stocks to squeeze out speculators targeting the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit by shorting the blue-chip Hang Seng Index. \par \par \uc2  The newspaper quoted Yam as warning that the clash with speculators targeting the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit by shorting the HSI would be "a long-term battle". \par \par \uc2  The local stock market has gained 14% since the government first targeted speculators last Friday. \par \par \uc2  But the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under renewed fire from a former executive with Chase Manhattan Bank in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  who sharply criticized the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a letter to the business section of the South China Morning Post. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 20-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0107GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8