\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Early -2: Yen Strength Helping HK Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1998\par 03:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is stronger and forwards are down early Wednesday helped by strength in the Japanese yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0100 GMT (9:00 p.m. EDT Tuesday), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7477 against the U.S. dollar, stronger than the HK$7.7495 quoted late Tuesday. The Hong Kong dollar has traded in a range of HK$7.7475 and HK$7.7483 so far Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the six-month premium is quoted at 2,400 points, down from 2,600 previously. The one-year premium is quoted at 4,900 points, down from 5,400 previously. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the strength in the yen, which is quoted at 144.08 per U.S. dollar in local trade is helping sentiment. \par \par \uc2  The yen's strength coincides with comments from Japanese officials hinting at support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The head of the international bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Haruhiko Kuroda, said Wednesday that an excessively strong dollar and weak yen are undesirable. Eisuke Sakakibara, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters that the opportunity for yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is getting near. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Interbank Offered Rates is quoted at 8.625%, compared with 9.50% late during the previous session. The three-month rate is 11.125% from 12.125% late Tuesday. For more Hibor news, please refer to Telerate page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 