central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The Philippine peso, however, failed to benefit from the\par regional rebound, with the U.S. dollar ending domestic\par trading at 42.920 pesos (PHP), up from PHP42.850 at the\par previous close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  08-19-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0747EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8j020pl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
