\par\par \b \uc2  JGBs weaker midday Tokyo as stocks rebound. \b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 04:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 18 (Reuters) - Key September 10-year Japanese government bond futures were weaker by midday on Tuesday due to a sharp rise in Tokyo share prices, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Euroyen futures were also firmer due to a rise in banking-sector shares, but trade was light, as traders looked to moves in the Hong Kong stock market for clues to direction. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  shares rose on Friday due to government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and there is concern about whether such rises can be sustained," a trader for a foreign brokerage said. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong stock market, which was closed on Monday for a holiday, resumed trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Hang Seng Index, which soared 8.47 percent to close at 7,224.69 points on Friday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock market to fend off \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators, opened at 7,246.75 points on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A fall in the Hang Seng could undermine the firmness of Tokyo share prices, which were cheered by overnight gains in U.S. stocks, traders said. \par \par \uc2  September JGB futures stood at 134.33 by midday, down from Monday's close of 134.38. Turnover was a light 17,776 lots. \par \par \uc2  Key 182nd 10-year JGB yield stood at 1.160 percent as of 0206 GMT, up from Monday's close of 1.150 percent. \par \par \uc2  Traders said bond and stock prices were likely to move in inverse relation to each other as long as short-term rates remained stable. \par \par \uc2  But they said extreme falls in share prices may raise concern about rises in money rates and profit-taking in bonds. \par \par \uc2  "If share prices fall too sharply, to say around the 14,500 to 14,000 points, concern about profit-taking in bonds may be heightened," said a trader for a city bank's securities unit. \par \par \uc2  In the Tokyo stock market, the key Nikkei 225 average stood at 15,091.81 at midday, up 2.01 percent or 297.15 from Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  Key March euroyen futures stood at 99.26 as of 0209 GMT, up from Monday's settlement of 99.24. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said euroyen futures were supported by reports by Kyodo news agency and Yomiuri Shimbun on Monday saying the government will use public funds to facilitate a merger between the Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan and Sumitomo Trust. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Tuesday there was no truth in the reports that the government had decided on such use of public funds. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan left a fund surplus of 1.2 trillion yen at 0020 GMT. Key call money stood at 0.35 percent as of 0214 GMT, down from Monday's weighted average of 0.41 percent. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473 3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8i010su\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
