\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards end up on rouble woes. \b0\par\par\uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 12:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab Close\tab \tab     Open\tab \tab Previous Close\par HK$ SPOT    7.7487/07\tab \tab 7.7489/99\tab   7.7495/00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  FORWARDS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3-Month\tab 1,270-1,320\tab     1,150-1,250\tab 930-1,000\par 6-Month\tab 2,600-2,700\tab     2,450-2,550    2,125-2,225\par 1-Year\tab  5,300-5,600\tab     5,050-5,250    4,450-4,650\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INTERBANK RATE (IN PERCENTAGE)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight     9.00-9.25\tab \tab 8.25-8.75\tab  7.50-8.00\par 3-Month     11.70-12.25\tab     11.10-11.62     10.50-11.00\par 6-Month     11.80-12.37\tab     11.70-12.25     11.10-11.60\par 1-year\tab 11.50-12.50\tab     11.70-12.25     11.90-12.50.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Aug 18 (Reuters) - US/HK forwards ended sharply higher on Tuesday despite last Friday's government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the stock and future market to fend off speculative attacks on the Hong Kong dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers attributed the higher rates to the Russian rouble devaluation which took regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets by surprise on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Since the (Hong Kong) financial market was closed on Monday, the market just started to feel the pain only today," a dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' reaction to Russia has been subdued after they tumbled on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Many bankers had hoped to unload some of their Hong Kong dollar funds accumulated last week as the expected major speculative attack on the Hong Kong dollar during the weekend did not materialise, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But many of these banks had held back as a result of Monday's rouble devaluation, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Banks were not very eager lending money today," said Stephen Yau, treasurer at ING Baring in Hong Kong.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said rates above one-month would stay firm in double digits in the near term, with the rouble devaluation outweighing the effect of last Friday's government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ward off a speculative attack on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said rates could have gone higher on Tuesday without the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  government had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last Friday, and if we still had a rouble devaluation yesterday, the Hang Seng Index would probably have plunged below 6,000 today and local interbank rates might have risen to 15 percent," said Peter Mak, treasurer at Belgian Bank in Hong Kong.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local forward market, trading was thin with moderate position-squaring, which indicated that most key players had not unwound their long dollar positions despite the government's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the stock and future markets last Friday, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China-backed banks were heard selling dollar forwards.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But they were offering forwards to a selected group of banks. Some banks suspected of being involved in speculative attacks against the Hong Kong dollar were heard to be not on their list," a dealer at a major bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The interbank rate yield curve has shifted up, helping to buoy the Hong Kong dollar spot.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The overnight rate was trading at two percentage points over the offer rate for the discount window at the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some said the yield curve would become flatter, as higher longer-dated rates would continue to fuel upward pressure on short term rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A treasurer said the overnight rate could hope to resume a downward bias, given the continued existence of the discount window.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Angi Li (852) 2847 4039; Fax 2845 0636.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8i00zog\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
