\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards hold gains by midday in thin trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,077 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 07:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab Midday\tab \tab    Open\tab \tab Previous Close\par HK$ SPOT    7.7485/05\tab \tab 7.7489/99\tab  7.7495/00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  FORWARDS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3-Month     1,200-1,300\tab     1,150-1,250\tab 930-1,000\par 6-Month     2,450-2,650\tab     2,450-2,550    2,125-2,225\par 1-Year\tab 5,100-5,400\tab     5,050-5,250    4,450-4,650\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INTERBANK RATE (IN PERCENTAGE)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight    8.50-8.62\tab \tab 8.25-8.75\tab   7.50-8.00\par 3-Month     11.50-12.00\tab     11.10-11.62     10.50-11.00\par 6-Month     11.70-12.25\tab     11.70-12.25     11.10-11.60\par 1-year\tab 12.20-12.75\tab     11.70-12.25     11.90-12.50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Aug 18 (Reuters) - US/HK forwards held early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains by midday on Tuesday despite last Friday's government\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the stock and futures market to fend off\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculative attacks on the Hong Kong dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers attributed the sharp gain in forwards to Russia's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par devaluation of the rouble on Monday when the local money market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was closed for a public holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the right time last Friday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but the overall market sentiment doesn't favour the long Hong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Kong dollar position," a senior dealer at a major European bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  government had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday, and if we still had a rouble devaluation yesterday, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hang Seng Index would probably have plunged below 6,000 today\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the local interbank rates might have risen to 15 percent,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said Peter Mak, treasurer at Belgian Bank in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the timing of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was appropriate but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par questioned whether it would be effective in fending off attacks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the long run.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Speculators are always around. If they don't attack it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar) today, they may do so tomorrow. Japan has\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  many times to boost the yen over the past few years,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and see what happened," a senior dealer at another European\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said that although forwards rose sharply over the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par long weekend, partly because of the rouble devaluation, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par scale of selling of the Hong Kong dollar was much smaller than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected and trading remained thin, exaggerating moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers had expected earlier there could be major selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the Hong Kong dollar during the long weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In the local money market trading activity was thin in both\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the forward and interbank markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We did not see much activity by the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this morning, except for some routine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offering term money after the government bills tender on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday," a dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the forwards market, some U.S. investment banks were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par heard both on the bid and offer side of the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forwards, while China-backed banks were heard mainly on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offer side taking a long position on the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But I heard the Chinese banks were offering selectively in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the forward market," one senior dealer at a major European bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rafael Hui, Secretary for Financial Services, said on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday selling of local dollars had continued, but the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government would only consider \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the securities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and futures market when there was a corresponding "play" on the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  side.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The objective is to provide a response to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 'play' in other words, betting against the Hong Kong dolar,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hui said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Aug 18 (Reuters) - US/HK forwards held early gains by midday on Tuesday despite last Friday's government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the stock and futures market to fend off speculative attacks on the Hong Kong dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers attributed the sharp gain in forwards to Russia's devaluation of the rouble on Monday when the local money market was closed for a public holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the right time last Friday, but the overall market sentiment doesn't favour the long Hong Kong dollar position," a senior dealer at a major European bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  government had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last Friday, and if we still had a rouble devaluation yesterday, the Hang Seng Index would probably have plunged below 6,000 today and the local interbank rates might have risen to 15 percent," said Peter Mak, treasurer at Belgian Bank in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the timing of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was appropriate but questioned whether it would be effective in fending off attacks on the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the long run.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Speculators are always around. If they don't attack it (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar) today, they may do so tomorrow. Japan has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  many times to boost the yen over the past few years, and see what happened," a senior dealer at another European bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said that although forwards rose sharply over the long weekend, partly because of the rouble devaluation, the scale of selling of the Hong Kong dollar was much smaller than expected and trading remained thin, exaggerating moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers had expected earlier there could be major selling of the Hong Kong dollar during the long weekend. The territory's financial markets were closed for a public holiday on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market trading activity was thin in both the forward and interbank markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We did not see much activity by the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this morning, except for some routine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of offering term money after the government bills tender on Tuesday," a dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the forwards market, some U.S. investment banks were heard both on the bid and offer side of the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forwards, while China-backed banks were heard mainly on the offer side taking a long position on the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But I heard the Chinese banks were offering selectively in the forward market," one senior dealer at a major European bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rafael Hui, Secretary for Financial Services, said on Tuesday selling of local dollars had continued, but the government would only consider \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the securities and futures market when there was a corresponding "play" on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  side.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The objective is to provide a response to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  'play' in other words, betting against the Hong Kong dolar," Hui said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He added: "Our intention is not to prop up the securities and futures market."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He also said the market should not overreact to the rouble woes.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Angi Li (852) 28847 4039; Fax 2845 0636.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8i00z1l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
