\par\par \b \uc2  HK$ Bond Ylds Rise On Higher Interbank Rates; 1Y Yld 10.25% \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 12:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong bond yields are higher late Tuesday on a rise in local interbank rates as local markets react with nervousness to the government's continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock market. \par \par \uc2  Late Tuesday, one-year Exchange Fund bills were yielding 10.25%, up from 9.90% late in the previous session. One-month bills were yielding 9.60%, up from 8.90% late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong markets were closed Monday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  Local interbank rates rose Tuesday amid nervousness over the government's new policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock market to scare away \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators, market participants said. \par \par \uc2  The overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate was quoted at 9.5% late Tuesday, up from 8.0% late in the previous session. The three-month rate was quoted at 12.125%, up from 11.25% late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  government last Friday announced its first ever \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock and stock futures market and continued buying the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to fend off speculators. The government continued to buy shares in blue-chip companies during Tuesday's session, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0953 GMT (5:53 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar was trading at HK$7.7491 per U.S. dollar, stronger than HK$7.7495 in London on Monday. \par \par \uc2  For more information on Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market activity, bill and note prices and other related information, please refer to Telerate page [9888]. \par \par \uc2  - By Jeffrey Timmermans; (852) 2802-7002; \par \par \uc2  jeffrey.timmermans@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 18-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1014GMT \par \par \uc2  4178 5096 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8i070nm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
