\par\par \b \uc2  HK$ Seen Steady In Thin Trade -2: Hibor Rates Climb \b0\par\par\uc2 224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 03:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers said forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums fell after profit taking, but they expect them to remain high for the moment. "I don't see room for higher rates from this point on but there's not much room to fall," said a dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  She predicted the Hong Kong dollar will trade between HK$7.7485 and HK$7.7498 per U.S. dollar. That's close to HK$7.7500, which is seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A dealer with an Australian bank predicted that the market will stay thin and skittish Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said last week's government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the stock market and the peg sent a signal to speculators that the stock market and peg are vulnerable to further attack. \par \par \uc2  Speculative moves on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the stock market forced interbank interest rates higher. They're now higher than they were Friday. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 8.5%, up from 8.0% Friday. The benchmark three-month rate is quoted at 12.25%, up from 11.25% previously. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852)2802-7002; \par \par \uc2  sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 18-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0134GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8i06ywa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
