\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP/HK Markets/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2: No HKMA Moves Seen Tuesday \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 12:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't seen in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Tuesday, but neither were speculators believed to be particularly active. For several sessions last week, the HKMA bought spot Hong Kong dollars to counter speculators who were selling the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  short in the forward market. \par \par \uc2  Still, while the spot Hong Kong dollar exchange rate was generally stable Tuesday at HK$7.7495, interest rates climbed as banks tightened lending, and forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums - though down from late Monday's levels in London - climbed from earlier in the day on increased hedging activity by nervous investors. \par \par \uc2  Late Tuesday, the overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 9.5%, up from 8% Friday. The three-month rate is quoted at 12.125%, up from 11.25% previously. \par \par \uc2  The devaluation of the Russian ruble had little impact on Hong Kong's markets Tuesday, though it taxed to another degree investors' already frayed faith in the government's ability to maintain the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's link to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Though the government didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Tuesday, the battle lines drawn Friday remain in place and are likely to be tested again, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The government said it's not opposed to speculators short-selling Hang Seng Index Futures or selling the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  short in the forward foreign market, but won't tolerate the two in concert because it puts a strain on the Hong Kong dollar peg. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 18-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1028GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8i070qe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
