\par\par \b \uc2  HK Govt/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2: Editorial Says Peg's Days Numbered \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1998\par 03:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Post said Secretary for Financial Services Rafael Hui noted that the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  began calling around to unspecified international bodies Friday, when the unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was announced. \par \par \uc2  He said \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted the international investment community to understand that the government hadn't "gone off the rails and was merely trying to prop up the market." \par \par \uc2  Markets reacted generally negatively to the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Hui said that was to have been expected. But the reaction was actually less severe than the government had foreseen. Hui told the Post the decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been an agonizing one. \par \par \uc2  Government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was supported over the weekend by the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Real Estate Developers Association, Lo Ka-shui, who is also the managing director of large property company, Great Eagle Holdings Ltd. \par \par \uc2  Lo accused international speculators of "front-running" in Hong Kong's markets in an attempt to cash in by hammering the local stock market and trying to break the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "It is essential the government maintain fair play in a free market; sometimes it means not allowing excessively powerful forces to play the insider game," Lo said. \par \par \uc2  Separately, the Post said in an unsigned Sunday editorial that "the most popular outlook is that the peg will be abandoned within the next six to 12 months," but didn't cite its sources. \par \par \uc2  Publicly, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants are unwilling to criticize the HKMA and the Hong Kong government and all say they believe the peg will stay. \par \par \uc2  But off the record, many participants say they believe the question is when, rather than whether the government will cave in to speculators and abandon the link. \par \par \uc2  In its editorial, the Post noted that Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peg "has done nothing to reverse the growing consensus that the peg's days are numbered." \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0112GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8h06yma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
