\par\par \b \uc2  Many HK papers back government market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1998\par 06:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Aug 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily newspapers on Saturday voiced support for the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock market on Friday, although some warned the move aimed at deflecting speculators could backfire. \par \par \uc2  Chinese language papers, the Apple Daily, Sing Pao, the Hong Kong Commercial Daily and the independent Ming Pao newspapers all agreed that an extraordinary move was needed to cope with an extraodinary crisis. \par \par \uc2  The Apple Daily warned that the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would bring side effects and noted that in effect the government had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets and used taxpayers money to gamble. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the territory's stock market for the first time, effectively supporting a flailing market but raising eyebrows over whether Hong Kong truly remained a free market. \par \par \uc2  The Hang Seng Index surged 8.47 percent on Friday, after hitting a five-year low on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong leaders repeatedly stressed they had not abandoned their hands-off policy in the markets, despite Friday's unprecedented action and the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ongoing purchases of Hong Kong dollars outside the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong Commercial Daily said the move would stabilise financial markets, a cornerstone for reviving the economy. \par \par \uc2  Pro-China papers, the Da Tung Pao and Wen Wei Po, also supported the move, noting that the government had successfully hit back at speculators and taught them a lesson. \par \par \uc2  Some of the dailies were less supportive, however. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong Economic Journal disagreed with the defence. The paper pointed out the HKMA was behaving like a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had upset \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial management principles and would have a long term effect on the market. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8f036ww\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
