\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-HK govt buys shares to foil speculators. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrea Ricci \par \uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 15:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Aug 14 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the territory's stock market for the first time on Friday, but officials said their aim was to foil speculators, not prop up the sagging market. \par \par \uc2  "The government has no intention to artificially support the stock market. The measures we have taken today are directed against specifically speculative activities," Hong Kong Chief Executive Tung Chee-hwa told reporters at a hastily called news conference. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, a grim-looking Financial Secretary Donald Tsang announced he had asked the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) to launch "counter activities in the stock and futures market" against speculators that had attacked the Hong Kong dollar as a means to influence stock prices. \par \par \uc2  Officals refused to disclose how much the HKMA spent buying shares and futures contracts. \par \par \uc2  Last week, overseas investment houses and hedge funds sold billions of U.S. dollars worth of Hong Kong dollars in both the spot and forward markets. \par \par \uc2  Conventional wisdom has it that speculators are not really targetting the Hong Kong dollar when they sell it. \par \par \uc2  Rather, they are trying to push up rates and cause stock prices to fall, either because they already have shorted the share market or want to buy stocks at cheaper prices. \par \par \uc2  Tsang said that was exactly what happened in the latest attack. \par \par \uc2  "This would enable them to benefit from their very substantial short positions which they have accumulated in the Hang Seng Index futures market," said Tsang. \par \par \uc2  Tsang said the government had no evidence past attacks on the Hong Kong dollar were linked to speculation in stocks. \par \par \uc2  "This is the first time we've \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the securities market because this is the first time we have seen a double play working against us in a critical time when regional confidence is fragile, when people wish to be reassured," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong leaders stressed repeatedly that they had not abandoned their hands-off policy in the markets, despite today's unprecedented action and the HKMA's ongoing purchases of Hong Kong dollars outside the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system. \par \par \uc2  "Our long-standing policy of non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock and futures markets remain unchanged," said Tsang. \par \par \uc2  He said the government would only contemplate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it believed movements in stock and futures markets were caused by rate hikes engineered by speculators. \par \par \uc2  Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, pressures for a weaker Hong Kong dollar automatically cause interest rates to rise and vice versa. Higher rates take a toll on asset markets and the real economy. \par \par \uc2  While most analysts say they expect the peg to stay, government actions to stabilize property prices and boost liquidity in the banking sector have raised questions about its willingness to take the pain of plummeting asset prices. \par \par \uc2  The latest massive attack on the Hong Kong dollar was foiled without a surge in interest rates because the HKMA purchased the local dollar for the government treasury, skirting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system and recirculating the dollars back into the banking system. \par \par \uc2  The treasury needed the funds to fill a shortfall, but the move nevertheless was viewed by some as a convenient tactic by the government to avoid rate rises. \par \par \uc2  Analysts took a jaded view of Friday's stock market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It won't change a thing. I think they (the speculators) will come back with a vengeance," said Steven Thompson, chief analyst at Nikko Research Center. \par \par \uc2  "They may have achieved a certain goal of burning these speculators, but at the same time they have probably damaged Hong Kong's reputation," said Thompson. \par \par \uc2  The Hang Seng Index surged 8.47 percent to 7,224.69 on Friday after hitting a five-year low on Thursday, but Hong Kong shares traded in London fell modestly after the government's announcement. ((Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371; Fax (852) 2845-0636 \par \par \uc2  hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8e036h7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
