\par\par \b \uc2  HK govt to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  if HK$ attacked repeatedly. \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Aug 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Financial Secretary Donald Tsang said on Friday the government would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar came under repeated attack, and the government had ample resources to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The government would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  under very specific circumstances which involved repeated attacks on the Hong Kong dollar while speculators were also present in the futures market, he told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock and futures market on Friday to foil speculators. \par \par \uc2  Tsang declined to describe the HKMA's actions or specify the scale of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but said \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sufficient resources in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to deal with speculative activities. \par \par \uc2  Tsang said Hong Kong's commitment to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board was "paramount". The Hong Kong dollar has been pegged to the U.S. dollar at HK$7.8 per dollar since 1983. \par \par \uc2  "(If) what we are dealing with is a very exceptional circumstance, then we have to deploy our foreign reserves to deal with very specific attacks on the Hong Kong dollar through a very unconventional means," Tsang said. \par \par \uc2  "We are not going to abandon the (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board) system... We have total resolve and we are going through all motions to defend the linked exchange," he added. \par \par \uc2  - Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6369; Fax (852) 2845 0636 \par \par \uc2  - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8e035o6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
