\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards end lower, fear of HK$ attack fades. \b0\par\par\uc2 661 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 12:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  Close\tab      Open\tab      Previous Close\par HK$ SPOT     7.7495/00\tab  7.7490/00\tab 7.7495/00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  FORWARDS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3-Month\tab 930-1,000     1,100-1,200    1,200-1,300\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 6-Month    2,125-2,225     2,400-2,500    2,700-2,800\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1-Year     4,450-4,650     4,800-5,100    5,100-5,400\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INTERBANK RATE (IN PERCENTAGE)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight   7.50-8.00\tab  8.50-9.00\tab 8.25-8.75\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3-Month    10.50-11.00     12.11-12.50    11.70-12.25\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 6-Month    11.10-11.60     11.75-12.25    12.00-12.50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1-Year     11.90-12.50     12.00-12.50    12.20-13.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Aug 14 (Reuters) - US/HK forwards posted sharp\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par falls by Friday's close as fears of a resumption of attacks on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Hong Kong dollar over the weekend faded on a powerful rally\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the local stock market and a stronger yen, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "It doesn't look like there is going to be an attack on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hong Kong dollar during the weekend. Activities were mainly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par focused on position-squaring today," said a senior dealer at a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par major U.S. commercial bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some key market players were heard taking profit on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/yen as well as on US/HK forwards, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers also said they did not notice any substantial borrowing interest from key players for short term and medium term money that they might need to fund positions on the Hong Kong dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The blue-chip Hang Seng Index staged a powerful rally, in part because of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the stock market by local government, rising by 564.27 points, or 8.47 percent, to 7,224.69 points on Frdiay.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the stock and futures market on Friday to foil speculators, Financial Secretary Donald Tsang told reporters after the market closed on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the government would contemplate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the stock and future markets only when there was sufficient reason to believe that movements in both markets are clearly and substantially caused by corresponding movements in interest rates engineered by speculative activities against the Hong Kong dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As far as the money market is concerned, the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was rumored to have offered one to three-month term funds into the interbank market while a note-issuing bank was heard offering one-month in moderate amounts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China-backed banks were widely seen as big lenders across the yield curve. Local interbank rates dropped by 30-120 basis points across the board on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hong Kong financial markets will be closed next Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers had warned earlier of a possible resumption of a major sell-off of the Hong Kong dollar during the weekend, when trading activity would be thin, helping to exaggerate moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Next week, the territory will mark the first anniversary of a major speculative attack against the Hong Kong dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The expiry of a large amount of US/HK forwards and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options next week could imply players with short positions against the Hong Kong dollar would lose money if the Hong Kong dollar peg held, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "After Donald Tsang's speech, I am sure there will not be a speculative attack against the Hong kong dollar during the weekend," Stephen Cheung, a director at Jardine Fleming Bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Local interbank rates were likely to stabilise in coming weeks, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cheung also said he would not expect a substantial upside of the dollar/yen in near term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This was mainly because of a series of high-level international exchanges due in the near future, including Chinese President Jiang Zemin's visit to Japan in September plus meetings between U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin and Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa, Cheung said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Angi Li (852) 2847 4039; Fax 2845 0636.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8e03558\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
