\par\par \b \uc2  US stocks firm but off highs,  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  fears ease. \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 17:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Aug 14 (Reuters) - U.S. stocks were off earlier highs but still firm Friday morning, reassured by words and actions in support of Asian and Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1109 EDT/1509 GMT, the Dow industrials were up 67 points to 8526. Blue chips had risen nearly 100 points at the open. Almost half of the Dow's gains came from a surge in J.P. Morgan  shares on reports it may merge with a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Morgan was up 9-1/8 at 125-15/16. \par \par \uc2  "Hong Kong is moving to stabilise its markets," said Jack Shaughnessy, chief investment strategist at Advest. \par \par \uc2  "It is not going to sit on its hands passively and allow market forces to dictate the direction of their markets." \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's Hang Seng index closed up 8.47 percent after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock and futures market to foil speculators. \par \par \uc2  Russian share and debt markets recovered after several days of panic-stricken declines. President Boris Yeltsin soothed nerves by vowing not to devalue the rouble. \par \par \uc2  In Japan, vice finance minister Eisuke Sakakibara said authorities were looking for a chance to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the yen. \par \par \uc2  "Deflationary fears are what is driving financial markets - bonds up and stocks down," Shaughnessy said. \par \par \uc2  The long bond was up 15/32 to yield 5.56 percent, firming with dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  Among the most active stocks, shares in CIENA Corp.  and Tellabs Inc. which is buying CIENA, tumbled after CIENA warned of a shortfall in third-quarter revenues and earnings. \par \par \uc2  CIENA fell 16-11/16 to 54-3/8. Tellabs was off 11-15/16 at 59-7/8. \par \par \uc2  Both companies, whose shares were the most active on the Nasdaq stock market, make telecommunications equipment. \par \par \uc2  ((Marjorie Olster, 212-859-1730)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8e033vg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
