\par\par \b \uc2  HK Tung -2: Defends Two-Pronged Move By HKMA \b0\par\par\uc2 186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 12:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong's Chief Executive on Friday defended a two-pronged move by the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fend off speculators, saying it was necessary to speed the Special Administrative Region's economic adjustment process. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it had done several times this week, bought Hong Kong dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday and also used money from its Exchange Fund to buy blue-chip stocks and futures to avoid an interest rate spike that could have led to market panic and lined the pockets of speculators. \par \par \uc2  Tung said Hong Kong needs a stable interest rate environment if it is to recover from the ravages of the ongoing regional financial markets crisis and vowed the HKMA would strike against speculators again, if necessary. \par \par \uc2  He said the Hong Kong government made central government officials in Beijing aware of the HKMA's action, but that there was no consultation or approval-seeking. \par \par \uc2  The decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  was solely \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's, he said. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1056GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8e06yem\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
