\par\par \b \uc2  Mkt Participants Question Role of HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By J.R. Wu \par \uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 23:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Was it an act of desperation or an act of resolve? \par \par \uc2  That's what market participants were trying to decide about the unprecedented act Friday by \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the territory's equity, futures and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  While the move appeared to be well-timed - coming at the end of a volatile trading week and ahead of a three-day holiday in Hong Kong - \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders and analysts remained uncertain if the action will mean the eventual delinking of the Hong Kong dollar to its U.S. counterpart. That could further roil already skittish global markets. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA), the territory's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , spent an undisclosed amount of its $96.5 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to buy Hang Seng's blue-chip stocks, index futures and Hong Kong dollars. \par \par \uc2  It was the first time ever the HKMA's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were used to buy local equities - an action as unfathomable as the U.S. Federal Reserve using its reserves to buy shares of stocks included in the Dow Jones Industrial Average. \par \par \uc2  "It looks kind of desperate," said Eric Nickerson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Bank of America in New York. "It shows that a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board is not something they are willing to live with." \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is pegged to the U.S. dollar with the HKMA effectively acting as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board to maintain the peg. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has thus far survived the rounds of devaluation and the freefall that has touched neighboring regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the onset of last year's Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  "When you \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , you are showing you have problems," said Stan Shipley, senior economist with Merrill Lynch in New York. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-08-98 \par \par \uc2  2125GMT \par \par \uc2  4227 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8e06xgv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
