\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Midday Flat; Forwards Ease Ahead Of Monday Holiday \b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 06:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is flat amid moderate trading at midday Friday, with banks squaring their positions ahead of a long holiday weekend in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  Dealers added that the Hong Kong dollar forwards \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates generally are easing in line with lower interbank lending rates and a rebound in the Hong Kong stock market. Before midday, the key index was up 4.9%. \par \par \uc2  Around 0400 GMT (12:00 a.m EDT, Friday), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7498 against the U.S. dollar, little changed from late Thursday's HK$7.7499. Trading has remained in a narrow range of between HK$7.7495 and HK$7.7500 in morning trade. The level of HK$7.7500 is seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, the six-month premium is quoted at 2,200 points, down from 2,650 late Thursday. The one-year premium is quoted at 4,900 points, down from 5,200 previously. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 14-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0413GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8e06wsz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
