\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA Sold/U.S Dlrs -2: Bks Urged To Be Prudent In Lending \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1998\par 13:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Thursday confirmed it had sold a "small amount" of U.S. dollars for Hong Kong dollars during the day, in what it called a "normal transaction." \par \par \uc2  The quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the transaction was done on behalf of the government to help it meet cash needs. An HKMA spokesman said it wasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The HKMA has described its recent activity as being related to the government's expected fiscal deficit of HK$21 billion in the current year. The HKMA manages the Hong Kong government's reserves money. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts aren't buying the HKMA claim and see the activity as straightforward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  By cooling the market through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the HKMA is preventing spikes in interest rates that would result because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system that Hong Kong operates, according to market participants. \par \par \uc2  There also are rumors in the market that some Hong Kong banks have had difficulting funding themselves on the interbank market because they have lent heavily to investment houses speculating on the dollar, the spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  While banks are free to make such loans, the HKMA advises them "to be very conscious of the funding and interest rate risks if they lend out sizable amounts of Hong Kong dollars without pre-funding themselves," the spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  In a somewhat veiled threat, the HKMA's statement reminded banks that when it lends in the market, the authority "takes into account the credit standing" of borrowers. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA operates a discount window as lender of last resort in the local money market, but at times has refused to deal with some banks that it suspects of funding speculators. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 13-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1143GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8d06vsy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
