\par\par \b \uc2  HK Midday Hibor Up;  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Jitters Hit Sentiment \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1998\par 05:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates are higher midday as the local stock market and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  come under selling pressure and the Japanese yen remains shaky. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 8.0%, up from 7.0% late Wednesday. The three-month rate is 11.625% up from 11.5%. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a combination of a sagging stock market, vulnerable-looking regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  led by the yen are taking their toll on interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  At 0316 GMT (11:16 p.m. EDT, Wednesday) the blue chip Hang Seng Index is down 206.76 points, or 3.0%, to 6652.72. It has now lost 16.2% so far this month. \par \par \uc2  The market remains thin, with few willing to lend or borrow in such a volatile environment. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a local bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters are also increasing fears of a possible devaluation of the Chinese yuan. Attention is focused on the Hong Kong dollar, which is again flirting with HK$7.7500, seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While the HKMA was seen in the market in the previous session lending in the three months, there's been no sign of the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far today. \par \par \uc2  In the futures market, the three-month September Hibor contract is quoted at 88.15 for an underlying money market yield of 11.85%. That's up from 88.75 and 11.25% previously. It has moved between 88.05 with an underlying interest rate of 11.95% and 88.30, with a yield of 11.7% on volume of 1,060 lots. \par \par \uc2  Late Thursday, the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7499 per U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7483 recorded late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 13-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0338GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8d06tvs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
