\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Intervention \highlight\uc2  Leads Some To Question  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Peg \b0\par\par\uc2  By Adam S. Najberg, Staff Reporter \par \uc2 844 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1998\par 16:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones Online News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days has worried some analysts, who say it will slow the territory's recovery from the current turmoil and may indicate it isn't prepared to pay the price its commitment to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg will exact. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA - Hong Kong's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - has acknowledged buying Hong Kong dollars three times in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the past week, most recently on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  It claims it's merely selling U.S. dollars from reserves to fund an expected HK$21.4 billion budget deficit for the current fiscal year, and says the moves don't constitute \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the activity coincided with a build-up of speculative positions against the Hong Kong dollar in the forward market, which boosted the U.S. dollar to HK$7.7510 at one point last week, above the HK$7.7500 level where it typically steps in to cool the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Along with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have warned they will mount a spirited defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although they are secretive about exactly what they will do. \par \par \uc2  "I cannot provide details of the strategies, because when we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fight against speculators, we would need some element of mystery," Financial Secretary Donald Tsang Yam-kuen said Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  But those threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and talk of a mystery arsenal, worry some market participants. They say the HKMA is overstepping its role as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board custodian and, ironically, giving speculators who hope to break the peg a reason to stick around. \par \par \uc2  "You don't need a secret arsenal if a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board works," says Desmond Supple, BZW's head of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research. "It has domestic economic implications and is particularly alarming to me. That suggests the political will is not strong enough for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board to work." \par \par \uc2  Because of Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board mechanism, the government has in theory given up control of monetary policy. If speculators sell the Hong Kong dollar, interest rates should rise automatically until they are high enough to attract buyers back to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  That's why critics like Supple are questioning why the HKMA has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past week to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and keep interest rates down. \par \par \uc2  Supple said HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is slowing \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic adjustment, since interest rates aren't being allowed to rise in line with market activity. \par \par \uc2  To some, that indicates that the territory won't stomach the havoc temporarily high interest rates will reap on the stock and property markets. The territory's main stock index, the Hang Seng, has already fallen 17% this month and 60% since last August, while property values have dropped 40% since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  With the government having suspended land sales until at least the end of the current fiscal year - another effort to help cushion the blow to the property market - it has been the Hang Seng Index that has born the brunt of asset price deflation. Several market analysts have said the index - trading at about 6600 points - is nearing its bottom. \par \par \uc2  When it can't get any lower, speculators who are shorting the stock index may well turn their attention back to the Hong Kong dollar, they said. \par \par \uc2  Still, SG Securities' Clive McDonnell said the HKMA is "caught between a rock and a hard place." He says the authority will be criticized for being too \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it steps into markets to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, or for destroying confidence in the peg if it doesn't. \par \par \uc2  He also said he believes rumors of speculation in recent weeks have been overblown and it makes sense for the HKMA to buy local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the government at this time of year because of its funding needs. \par \par \uc2  And sources close to Soros Fund Management, which was blamed for a speculative move on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, said finger-pointers should point elsewhere. \par \par \uc2  But speculators are out there, and the government is remaining vigilant. That means interest rates will remain at high levels and the economy will continue to bear the pain of the linked exchange rate, BZW's Supple said. \par \par \uc2  Traders Thursday warned that there will be more battles between the government and speculators, the next perhaps Friday, ahead of a three-day weekend in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  And with each battle, the questions about how long the HKMA will be willing and able to keep the peg in place heat up. Even the staunchest believers are starting to ask themselves when, rather than whether, the government will abandon the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board it has kept in place for 15 years. \par \par \uc2  "The only way you can restore Hong Kong dollar wealth is by breaking the peg, and then \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  adjustments start to come into play," Supple said. \par \par \uc2  - Adam S. Najberg; (852)2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1998 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2  1145 4201 62552 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020329du8d015im\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
