\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards end lower as yen firms, HKMA offers. \b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 11:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab      Close\tab \tab Open\tab \tab Previous Close\par HK$ SPOT   7.7477/87\tab  7.7495/00\tab  7.7485/95\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  FORWARDS \par \par \uc2  3-Month    1,000-1,100     1,100-1,200     1,230-1,340 \par \par \uc2  6-Month    2,300-2,400     2,550-2,900     2,900-3,500 \par \par \uc2  1-Year     4,600-4,900     5,000-5,300     5,300-5,600 \par \par \uc2  INTERBANK RATE (IN PERCENTAGE) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight  6.50-7.00\tab  7.62-8.12\tab  7.00-8.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3-Month    11.00-11.50     11.50-12.00     12.30-13.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 6-Month    11.30-11.87     12.00-12.60     12.90-13.50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1-Year     11.10-12.12     12.50-13.00     12.80-13.60.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Aug 12 (Reuters) - A fall in interbank rates, mainly on term money offers by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and renewed hope of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost the yen triggered long dollar liquidation in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forwards, dealers said on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Forwards with maturities between three-month and one-year slid by 100 to 700 points on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The HKMA was heard offering three-month term money, and on top of that, there is significant lending interest in the three-month and above," a dealer at a major commercial bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said they had expected the HKMA would offer term money since it has bought large amounts of Hong Kong dollars, helping to defend the key support level of HK$7.75 after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under selling pressure last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China-backed banks, note-issuing banks and local banks were major lenders in the interbank market across the board, helping to keep rates soft, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the forward market, Japanese banks were heard on the bid side, while U.S. banks were heard on the offer side on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite lower interbank rates, the Hong Kong dollar spot reversed course and turned moderately stronger in late trade amid improved sentiment boosted by a stronger yen, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But they said the good mood on Wednesday was unlikely to last because the underlying tone of the Japanese yen was weak.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039; Fax 2845 0636.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8c02x80\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (hong kong near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row }